=== 5. CONCLUSION ===
HYPOTHESIS: The effect of SES (socioeconomic status) on BA degree completion is the one that changes: it is strongly positive (~+0.35 in log-odds, p<0.001) in a baseline logit with social-background controls, but flips to a small negative and statistically insignificant coefficient (~-0.23; p rises from <0.001 to 0.02-0.16 depending on SE convention) once race dummies and academic characteristics (ASVAB ability composite and class percentile; no curriculum measure exists in the data) are added. This indicates that the apparent positive association between socioeconomic status and earning a BA is explained away by academic achievement differentials across SES groups rather than by a direct causal effect of SES.
